 Only the unsupported-kind list changes among the prior method bodies.
 V15's measured 204.871 seconds leave limited headroom against the unchanged
 240-second run limit. V16 remains pending independent review and execution.
+
+## Forward V18: repeated Renew reaches the reserved Stop position
+
+The recorder may renew the same held fence through original position 15
+after the already committed Resume at position 3. Each Renew increments
+revision, binds its immediate committed head and the exact old and new
+fence versions, checks the previous expiry through COMMIT, and allocates
+one original operation identity. The acquired fence identity stays
+allocated once at position 2.
+
+The fresh command at would-be position 16 is still eligible for the
+ordinary budget check. The unchanged position predicate counts 15
+existing, one ordinary and one reserved Stop position and refuses at 17
+against 16. The remaining dependency charge fits exactly at 112 including
+both proposed operations. An independent upper check covers the other
+row, key and byte dimensions. The old hold is still live for this refusal.
+
+Original Stop at 16 selects the latest Renew Command and its exact current
+fence version, and independently resolves the original Resume Command at
+3. The prior Renew's Result cannot substitute for that earlier control
+pin. The complete history preserves the earlier fence versions. The
+position-15 getter closure has 58 pins and the Stop getter has 61. Stop
+clears the hold and advances revision from 13 to 14. The full scope has
+189 retained rows, 199 logical row writes and 398 logical keys, or 215
+row and 446 key touches including the pending originals.
+
+V18 adds one focused native test and keeps the earlier 36 test methods
+byte-identical. The unchanged authorization, broker, policy and budget
+remain within the private research package. A separate 240-second
+targeted run is pending. The bounded position witness and the existing
+structural byte proof are separate from a reachable byte maximum,
+physical capacity and broader hosted acceptance.
